{"abstract":[{"text":"Show a Markdown document in a SwiftUI view, and adapt it to light and dark mode.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DisplayingMarkdownWithSwiftUI"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"MarkdownKit"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Displaying Markdown with SwiftUI"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftUI comes with support for Markdown-formatted snippets but does not have a full-fledged viewer for Markdown documents. MarkdownKit includes a SwiftUI view for displaying Markdown documents. As opposed to many other custom created Markdown views, the one included in MarkdownKit is based on the CommonMark-compliant MarkdownKit parser as well as its attributed string generator. It is thus lightweight yet still quite configurable. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is available on macOS 14 and iOS 17 or later.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The initializer of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" receives the parsed Markdown content of type ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"waitingMessage:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter which defines what is being displayed while the content is being rendered (especially if many images need to be loaded), as well as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter defining how the parsed Markdown is transformed into an attributed string, which is then being shown in the view. The generator is not just called once, but every time the color scheme has changed to potentially update the colors in use.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A variant of this initializer accepts a Markdown document as a string and uses the extended Markdown parser internally to parse it (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" if you pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"full: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). There are two initializers for each of the two ways of providing the document. Either you pass a ","type":"text"},{"code":"generator:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or you do not provide one and the view uses the default generators for light and dark mode, which can be configured with ","type":"text"},{"code":"renderingOptions:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"; the default is ","type":"text"},{"code":".trusted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following code snippet shows the signatures of the initializers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct MarkdownText: View {","  init(_ text: Block,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       renderingOptions: AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions = .trusted,","       mermaid: MermaidConfig? = nil) {","    ...","  }","  init(_ text: Block,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       generator: ((Block, ColorScheme) -> NSAttributedString?)?) {","    ...","  }","  init(string: String,","       full: Bool = false,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       renderingOptions: AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions = .trusted,","       mermaid: MermaidConfig? = nil) {","    ...","  }","  init(string: String,","       full: Bool = false,","       waitingMessage: NSAttributedString = NSAttributedString(string: \"⏳\"),","       generator: ((Block, ColorScheme) -> NSAttributedString?)?) {","    ...","  }","  ...","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Keep-untrusted-content-in-check","level":3,"text":"Keep untrusted content in check","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view generates the attributed string synchronously, which is why only the rendering options ","type":"text"},{"code":"baseUrl","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"localImages","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"imageExtensions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"safeMode","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"textSizeMultiplier","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" have an effect (remote images are never loaded). Use ","type":"text"},{"code":"MarkdownText(string: text, renderingOptions: .untrusted)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if the Markdown does not come from a trusted source. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Show-Mermaid-diagrams","level":3,"text":"Show Mermaid diagrams","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid: .default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to draw diagrams. The view first shows the code of a diagram and replaces it with the diagram once it has been rendered in the background. In dark mode, it uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MermaidConfig/darkVariant","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Customize-the-generators-for-light-and-dark-mode","level":3,"text":"Customize the generators for light and dark mode","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Here is an example how view ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" could be used in a simple Markdown viewer. It defines an attributed string generator that uses two color schemes depending on whether dark mode is active or not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct ContentView: View {","  private static let lightGenerator = AttributedStringGenerator()","  private static let darkGenerator = AttributedStringGenerator(","      fontColor: \"#FFF\", codeFontColor: \"#FFF\",","      codeBlockFontColor: \"#FF6\", codeBlockBackground: \"#333\",","      syntaxHighlighting: .defaultDark,","      borderColor: \"#BBB\", h1Color: \"#FFF\", h2Color: \"#FFF\",","      h3Color: \"#FFF\", h4Color: \"#FFF\")","  ","  let content = ExtendedMarkdownParser.standard.parse(\"\"\"","    Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, **consectetur adipiscing** elit. Aliquam","    non risus in massa ornare lacinia. _Etiam_ at ullamcorper ligula.","    ","    1. This is the first item","    2. This is the second item","    3. This is the third item","    ","    Cras laoreet tellus dolor, ac `suscipit augue` molestie a.","    Integer efficitur odio massa, in dictum arcu dictum in.","    ","    | Column 1           | Column 2          | Col 3 |","    | ------------------ | ----------------- | :---: |","    | Nunc at dignissim  | More `cell` text  | One   |","    | Integer **ligula** | Justo nec finibus | Two   |","    | Cras nibh ex       | Praesent congue   | Three |","    \"\"\")","  ","  var body: some View {","    MarkdownText(self.content) { doc, colorScheme in","      switch colorScheme {","        case .dark:","          return Self.darkGenerator.generate(doc: doc)","        default:","          return Self.lightGenerator.generate(doc: doc)","      }","    }","    .padding()","  }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit":{"abstract":[{"text":"Parse, process and display text in Markdown format.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"MarkdownKit","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator":{"abstract":[{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides functionality for converting Markdown blocks into","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects that are used in macOS and iOS for displaying rich text.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The implementation is extensible allowing subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"override how individual Markdown structures are converted into attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AttributedStringGenerator"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct":{"abstract":[{"text":"Options for rendering the HTML that ","type":"text"},{"code":"AttributedStringGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates into an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSAttributedString","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". They are used by the synchronous methods (","type":"text"},{"code":"generate(doc:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" etc.) as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"well as by the asynchronous ones (","type":"text"},{"code":"generateAsync(doc:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" etc.).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RenderingOptions"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator/RenderingOptions-swift.struct","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RenderingOptions"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AttributedStringGenerator.RenderingOptions","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/attributedstringgenerator/renderingoptions-swift.struct"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block":{"abstract":[{"text":"Enumeration of Markdown blocks. This enumeration defines the block structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"i.e. the abstract syntax, of Markdown supported by MarkdownKit. The structure of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inline text is defined by the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" struct.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Block","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Block"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Block","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/block"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/CustomizingAttributedStringOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Style the attributed strings that ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" creates, and understand what the system’s HTML importer does with the styles.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/CustomizingAttributedStringOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Customizing Attributed String Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/customizingattributedstringoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams":{"abstract":[{"text":"Show fenced code blocks with the language ","type":"text"},{"code":"mermaid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as diagrams in attributed strings.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/DrawingMermaidDiagrams","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Drawing Mermaid Diagrams","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/drawingmermaiddiagrams"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser":{"abstract":[{"code":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects are used to parse Markdown text represented as a string using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"all features of MarkdownKit: the syntax of the CommonMark specification and all extensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that MarkdownKit implements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/FullMarkdownParser","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FullMarkdownParser"}],"role":"symbol","title":"FullMarkdownParser","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/fullmarkdownparser"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput":{"abstract":[{"text":"Convert a parsed Markdown document into HTML, attributed strings, plain text or text for ANSI terminals.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Generating Output","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/generatingoutput"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText":{"abstract":[{"text":"A SwiftUI view that displays a Markdown document as formatted text. The view converts the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document into an attributed string with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/AttributedStringGenerator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", using different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"generators for light and dark mode, and shows the result in a read-only text view whose text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be selected. The view scrolls vertically.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownText"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MarkdownText","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MarkdownText"}],"role":"symbol","title":"MarkdownText","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/markdowntext"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MermaidConfig/darkVariant":{"abstract":[{"text":"The configuration to use for dark backgrounds if this one is meant for light backgrounds:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it uses the dark theme instead of ","type":"text"},{"code":".default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".neutral","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":".forest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A configuration","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which already uses ","type":"text"},{"code":".dark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":".base","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a theme for which the colors are set explicitly","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"via ","type":"text"},{"code":"themeVariables","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is returned unchanged.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"darkVariant"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11MarkdownKit13MermaidConfigV","text":"MermaidConfig"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/MermaidConfig/darkVariant","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"darkVariant","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/mermaidconfig/darkvariant"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown":{"abstract":[{"text":"Restrict what raw HTML, links and images in a document may do when the Markdown does not come from you.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/RenderingUntrustedMarkdown","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Rendering Untrusted Markdown","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/renderinguntrustedmarkdown"},"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text":{"abstract":[{"text":"Struct ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is used to represent inline text. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" struct consists of a sequence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"TextFragment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" objects.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"identifier":"doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Text","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Text","type":"topic","url":"/documentation/markdownkit/text"}},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/GeneratingOutput","doc://MarkdownKit/documentation/MarkdownKit/Custom